  "content": {
    "id": "p32-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "A cuboid of volume $36\\text{ cm}^3$ has dimensions $x\\text{ cm}\\times y\\text{ cm}\\times z\\text{ cm}$ where $x$, $y$ and $z$ are integers and $x<y<z$. Find the possible dimensions of this cuboid.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1\\text{ cm}\\times2\\text{ cm}\\times18\\text{ cm}$; $1\\text{ cm}\\times3\\text{ cm}\\times12\\text{ cm}$; $1\\text{ cm}\\times4\\text{ cm}\\times9\\text{ cm}$; $2\\text{ cm}\\times3\\text{ cm}\\times6\\text{ cm}$.\n\nList positive integer factor triples of $36$ with all three dimensions strictly increasing.",
      "worked": "$$xyz=36.$$\n\nIf $x\\ge3$, then $y\\ge4$ and $z\\ge5$, giving $xyz\\ge60$. Hence $x=1$ or $x=2$.\n\nFor $x=1$, the factor pairs $y<z$ of $36$ with $y>1$ are $(2,18)$, $(3,12)$ and $(4,9)$.\n\nFor $x=2$, $yz=18$ with $2<y<z$ gives $(y,z)=(3,6)$.\n\nThe dimensions are $1\\times2\\times18$, $1\\times3\\times12$, $1\\times4\\times9$ and $2\\times3\\times6$, each in centimetres.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 58
  },
